    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green: **262 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## What I changed\n\nIn `OwnerMapper.formatMembershipLevel` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`), I added a **tenure factor** for membership level 4:\n\n- Level still starts at 1, +1 for an email, +1 when `namesakeCount == 0`.\n- **New:** +1 when the owner's tenure exceeds 365 days, i.e. `registrationDate.plusDays(365).isBefore(LocalDate.now())`. This is a strict \"more than 365 days\" check \u2014 exactly 365 days does not qualify.\n- The cap was raised from `Math.min(level, 3)` to `Math.min(level, 4)`.\n\nBecause a newly created owner's `registrationDate` is the current date, its tenure is zero, so the tenure factor never fires for a new owner. The maximum a new owner can reach is therefore 3 (base + email + no-namesake), never 4 \u2014 exactly as the spec requires. The `AcceptanceTest.coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` case (new owner with email, `namesakeCount` 0) correctly returns level 3.\n\nI also updated the Javadoc to describe the 1\u20134 range and the tenure rule.",
